x.en:
The Risk register contains the contingency plans and triggers that call for their execution.

The risk register may include but is not limited to:

&middot; Agreed-upon response strategies;

&middot; Specific actions to implement the chosen response strategy;

&middot; Trigger conditions, symptoms, and warning signs of a risk occurrence;

&middot; Budget and schedule activities required to implement the chosen responses;

&middot; Contingency plans and risk triggers that call for their execution;

&middot; Fallback plans for use when a risk has occurred and the primary response proves to be inadequate;

&middot; Residual risks that are expected to remain after planned responses have been taken, as well as those that have been deliberately accepted; and

&middot; Secondary risks that arise as a direct outcome of implementing a risk response.

